      "id": "native-delivery",
      "module": "verify/native-delivery/NativeDelivery.tla",
      "claim": "A native sender publishes attempt intent before transport, retries exact bytes at the bound destination, preserves uncertain custody through refusal/reopen/resume, conserves attempt and outage evidence, and marks retention only after checking its exact receipt.",
      "status": "implementation-correspondence",
      "bounds": "One job; three foreign binding variants; two attempts per budget; one explicit resume; two classified outages; normal permits one interruption, uncertain-write permits two interruptions and one precommit outcome refusal.",
      "assumptions": [
        "Successful local transactions and barriers are atomic and durable. Interrupted unknown attempts remain charged; only durably classified outages restore the charge. No SQLite, filesystem or physical power-loss proof.",
        "Exact symbolic identities; valid receipts come from the modeled honest selected relay. Positions are finite equivalence-class representatives, including zero and above-i64::MAX cases. No cryptographic/refinement proof.",
        "Due abstracts eligibility; no backoff arithmetic, wall-clock, multi-job fairness, cancellation, deletion or delivery-liveness claim.",
        "The failed-outcome action covers only precommit refusal. Postcommit sync/readback failures may retain the outcome and are not modeled; completed publication followed by process interruption is covered separately."
      ],
